{"probe_id":"instr.format_compliance.L1.004","canonical_id":"instr.format_compliance","category":"instr","level":"L1","axis_values":{"wrapper_specificity":"markdown_table"},"prompt":"Render the following table as a markdown table with header row 'Animal | Legs', a separator row, and exactly three data rows. Use a leading and trailing vertical bar on every row. Data: dog has 4 legs; spider has 8 legs; ostrich has 2 legs. Output only the markdown table.","ground_truth":"format_only","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"header_sep_three_rows","regex":"^\\| *Animal *\\| *Legs *\\|\\n\\| *:?-+:? *\\| *:?-+:? *\\|\\n\\| *[A-Za-z]+ *\\| *\\d+ *\\|\\n\\| *[A-Za-z]+ *\\| *\\d+ *\\|\\n\\| *[A-Za-z]+ *\\| *\\d+ *\\|\\s*$"},{"name":"has_dog_4","regex":"\\bdog\\b[^\\n]*\\| *4 *\\|"},{"name":"has_spider_8","regex":"\\bspider\\b[^\\n]*\\| *8 *\\|"},{"name":"has_ostrich_2","regex":"\\bostrich\\b[^\\n]*\\| *2 *\\|"}]},"tags":["instruction_following","format_compliance"]}
