{"probe_id":"instr.keyword_avoidance.L2.001","canonical_id":"instr.keyword_avoidance","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"list_size":"few","topical_centrality":"central_to_topic"},"prompt":"Write a coherent 90-130 word piece about the appeal of vinyl records. Count words as non-whitespace tokens separated by whitespace. The words 'analog', 'warm', 'crackle', and 'turntable', in any capitalization, may not appear anywhere in your response. Output only the piece.","ground_truth":"A valid response must: (1) contain 90-130 whitespace-delimited non-whitespace tokens; (2) contain none of the forbidden words analog, warm, crackle, or turntable in any capitalization; (3) be a coherent piece that substantively discusses one or more appealing aspects of vinyl records; and (4) contain no surrounding commentary or labels.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Pass only if the response satisfies every content, formatting, counting, ordering, casing, preservation, and output-only constraint stated in this task. Treat literal/exact/verbatim requirements strictly. Task: Write a coherent 90-130 word piece about the appeal of vinyl records. Count words as non-whitespace tokens separated by whitespace. The words 'analog', 'warm', 'crackle', and 'turntable', in any capitalization, may not appear anywhere in your response. Output only the piece."],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["unit_test_required"]}
