{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L1.005","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L1","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"narrow","tempting_rewrites":"few"},"prompt":"Below is a sentence. Delete the word 'really' and change nothing else (preserve any double spaces if produced). Output only the modified sentence.\n\nOriginal: That was really quite unexpected.","ground_truth":"That was  quite unexpected.","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"That was  quite unexpected.","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[],"notes":"Note the double space after 'was' is intentional — delete the word, preserve spacing."}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L2.001","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"narrow","tempting_rewrites":"few"},"prompt":"Replace every occurrence of the word 'colour' (British spelling) with 'shade' in the passage below. Preserve all other British spellings, all punctuation choices (including the Oxford comma usage as written), and all line breaks. Do not 'fix' anything else. Output only the modified passage.\n\nPASSAGE:\nThe colour of the harbour was unusual that morning. Boats, gulls, and old fishermen drifted past, and the colour seemed to deepen.\nLater, a thin mist rose, and the colour shifted again.","ground_truth":"The shade of the harbour was unusual that morning. Boats, gulls, and old fishermen drifted past, and the shade seemed to deepen.\nLater, a thin mist rose, and the shade shifted again.","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exact_output","regex":"\\AThe\\ shade\\ of\\ the\\ harbour\\ was\\ unusual\\ that\\ morning\\.\\ Boats,\\ gulls,\\ and\\ old\\ fishermen\\ drifted\\ past,\\ and\\ the\\ shade\\ seemed\\ to\\ deepen\\.\\\nLater,\\ a\\ thin\\ mist\\ rose,\\ and\\ the\\ shade\\ shifted\\ again\\.\\Z"}]},"tags":["unit_test_required"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L2.002","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Replace every occurrence of 'gonna' with 'going to' in the passage below. Preserve all other informal spellings, contractions, and punctuation (including the run-on style). Do not 'fix' anything else. Output only the modified passage.\n\nPASSAGE:\nso i'm gonna head out early, gonna grab a coffee, and gonna see if marco is around — y'know how it is.\nhe's prolly gonna say no.","ground_truth":"so i'm going to head out early, going to grab a coffee, and going to see if marco is around — y'know how it is.\nhe's prolly going to say no.","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"so i'm going to head out early, going to grab a coffee, and going to see if marco is around — y'know how it is.\nhe's prolly going to say no.","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L2.003","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Replace every occurrence of the word 'foo' with 'bar' in the passage below. Preserve all original punctuation, capitalization, and any intentional ALL-CAPS words. Do not change anything else. Output only the modified passage.\n\nPASSAGE:\nThe foo went WEST. Then the foo went EAST. Finally, the foo stopped at the GATE — exhausted but unbroken. foo, foo, foo!","ground_truth":"The bar went WEST. Then the bar went EAST. Finally, the bar stopped at the GATE — exhausted but unbroken. bar, bar, bar!","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exact_output","regex":"\\AThe\\ bar\\ went\\ WEST\\.\\ Then\\ the\\ bar\\ went\\ EAST\\.\\ Finally,\\ the\\ bar\\ stopped\\ at\\ the\\ GATE\\ —\\ exhausted\\ but\\ unbroken\\.\\ bar,\\ bar,\\ bar!\\Z"}]},"tags":["instruction_following","preserve_constraint"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L2.004","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"narrow","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Replace every occurrence of 'organisation' with 'organization' in the passage below. Preserve all other British spellings (analyse, behaviour, traveller, etc.) exactly as written. Do not change anything else. Output only the modified passage.\n\nPASSAGE:\nThe organisation will analyse traveller behaviour at five centres. Each organisation must report by Tuesday. The organisation's data shall be archived without modification.","ground_truth":"The organization will analyse traveller behaviour at five centres. Each organization must report by Tuesday. The organization's data shall be archived without modification.","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"The organization will analyse traveller behaviour at five centres. Each organization must report by Tuesday. The organization's data shall be archived without modification.","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["instruction_following","preserve_constraint"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L2.005","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L2","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Replace every occurrence of 'dog' with 'hound' in the passage below. Preserve all original line breaks (including the trailing blank line at the end), punctuation, and capitalization. Do not change anything else. Output only the modified passage.\n\nPASSAGE:\nThe dog barked.\nThe dog ran.\nThe dog slept.\n\n","ground_truth":"The hound barked.\nThe hound ran.\nThe hound slept.\n\n","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"The hound barked.\nThe hound ran.\nThe hound slept.\n\n","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":false},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L3.001","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L3","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Convert the following CSV table into a Markdown table with the same column order. Preserve the exact raw text of every CSV field, including leading spaces, trailing punctuation, and capitalization. Treat the output as raw Markdown source: do not add any whitespace between a `|` delimiter and a field unless that whitespace is part of that CSV field. Use `|---|---|---|` as the separator row. Output only the table.\n\nCSV:\nName,Score,Notes\nAlice,  92, Final\nBob,87.,N/A\nCarol,95,GREAT","ground_truth":"|Name|Score|Notes|\n|---|---|---|\n|Alice|  92| Final|\n|Bob|87.|N/A|\n|Carol|95|GREAT|","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"|Name|Score|Notes|\n|---|---|---|\n|Alice|  92| Final|\n|Bob|87.|N/A|\n|Carol|95|GREAT|","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["unit_test_required"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L3.002","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L3","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Convert the following key=value lines into a JSON object. Preserve each value as a STRING exactly as written (do not coerce to numbers or booleans, do not trim whitespace, do not normalize). Output only the JSON object on a single line.\n\nINPUT:\nuser=  Alice\nage=42\nactive=TRUE\nemail=a@b.c","ground_truth":"{\"user\":\"  Alice\",\"age\":\"42\",\"active\":\"TRUE\",\"email\":\"a@b.c\"}","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Pass only if the response satisfies every content, formatting, counting, ordering, casing, preservation, and output-only constraint stated in this task. Treat literal/exact/verbatim requirements strictly. Task: Convert the following key=value lines into a JSON object. Preserve each value as a STRING exactly as written (do not coerce to numbers or booleans, do not trim whitespace, do not normalize). Output only the JSON object on a single line.\n\nINPUT:\nuser=  Alice\nage=42\nactive=TRUE\nemail=a@b.c"],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L3.003","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L3","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Convert the following pipe-delimited rows into a JSON array of objects with header keys 'sku','title','price'. Preserve every value EXACTLY as a string (do not parse the price as a number, do not strip leading $ or commas, do not change case). Output only the JSON array on one line.\n\nINPUT:\nsku|title|price\nA-01|Old Map|$1,250\nA-02|toy car|$ 9.99\nA-03|GLOVES|free","ground_truth":"[{\"sku\":\"A-01\",\"title\":\"Old Map\",\"price\":\"$1,250\"},{\"sku\":\"A-02\",\"title\":\"toy car\",\"price\":\"$ 9.99\"},{\"sku\":\"A-03\",\"title\":\"GLOVES\",\"price\":\"free\"}]","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Pass only if the response satisfies every content, formatting, counting, ordering, casing, preservation, and output-only constraint stated in this task. Treat literal/exact/verbatim requirements strictly. Task: Convert the following pipe-delimited rows into a JSON array of objects with header keys 'sku','title','price'. Preserve every value EXACTLY as a string (do not parse the price as a number, do not strip leading $ or commas, do not change case). Output only the JSON array on one line.\n\nINPUT:\nsku|title|price\nA-01|Old Map|$1,250\nA-02|toy car|$ 9.99\nA-03|GLOVES|free"],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L3.004","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L3","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"narrow","tempting_rewrites":"few"},"prompt":"Convert the following YAML-like key-value mapping into a TOML document. Treat the text after each colon as a raw scalar lexeme; do not parse or infer YAML types. Preserve each scalar's exact characters as a TOML string by wrapping it in double quotes. Output only the TOML, with key-value pairs in the same order as input, one per line, and no top-level table header.\n\nINPUT:\nname: 0042\nflag: yes\nnote: a, b, c","ground_truth":"name = \"0042\"\nflag = \"yes\"\nnote = \"a, b, c\"","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"name = \"0042\"\nflag = \"yes\"\nnote = \"a, b, c\"","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["instruction_following","preserve_constraint"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.preserve_constraint.L3.005","canonical_id":"instr.preserve_constraint","category":"instr","level":"L3","axis_values":{"transformation_scope":"broad","tempting_rewrites":"many"},"prompt":"Convert the following CSV row into an HTML <tr> with three <td> cells. Preserve each cell's content EXACTLY between the <td> tags (do not trim leading/trailing spaces, do not encode anything, do not change case). Output only the single <tr>...</tr> on one line.\n\nCSV:\n   widget , 17 , In Stock!  ","ground_truth":"<tr><td>   widget </td><td> 17 </td><td> In Stock!  </td></tr>","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"<tr><td>   widget </td><td> 17 </td><td> In Stock!  </td></tr>","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":false},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.case_uniformity.L1.001","canonical_id":"instr.case_uniformity","category":"instr","level":"L1","axis_values":{"target_case":"all_lower","casing_pressure":"proper_nouns_present"},"prompt":"Reply in all lowercase letters. Write a 30-50 word note about a quiet library. No capital letters anywhere. Count words as whitespace-separated tokens. Output only the note.","ground_truth":"format_only","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"all_lower_and_wc_30_50","regex":"^\\s*(?![\\s\\S]*[A-Z])\\S+(?:\\s+\\S+){29,49}\\s*$"}]},"tags":["unit_test_required"]}
{"probe_id":"instr.case_uniformity.L1.002","canonical_id":"instr.case_uniformity","category":"instr","level":"L1","axis_values":{"target_case":"all_upper","casing_pressure":"proper_nouns_present"},"prompt":"Reply in all UPPERCASE letters. Write a 25-45 word announcement about a SCHOOL BAKE SALE. Include the words SCHOOL, BAKE, and SALE. No lowercase letters anywhere. Output only the announcement.","ground_truth":"format_and_required_keywords","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"all_upper","regex":"^[^a-z]*$"},{"name":"contains_uppercase_letter","regex":".*[A-Z].*"},{"name":"wc_25_45","regex":"^(?:\\s*\\S+){25,45}\\s*$"},{"name":"contains_school","regex":"(?s).*\\bSCHOOL\\b.*"},{"name":"contains_bake","regex":"(?s).*\\bBAKE\\b.*"},{"name":"contains_sale","regex":"(?s).*\\bSALE\\b.*"}]},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"instr.case_uniformity.L1.003","canonical_id":"instr.case_uniformity","category":"instr","level":"L1","axis_values":{"target_case":"all_lower","casing_pressure":"proper_nouns_present"},"prompt":"reply using only lowercase ascii letters, spaces, and ordinary lowercase punctuation. write a 30-50 word description of a window seat on a train. output only the description.","ground_truth":"format_only","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"all_lower_ascii","regex":"^[^A-Z]*$"},{"name":"wc_30_50","regex":"^(?:\\s*\\S+){30,50}\\s*$"}],"notes":"This revision explicitly limits the casing requirement to ASCII, matching the regex. If the intended requirement is Unicode-wide lowercase, replace all_lower_ascii with a Unicode-aware uppercase-character check in scorer implementation."},"tags":[]}
